---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="alert-notify Documentation: Vue"
  description="Use alert-notify in Vue 3 with optional Toaster, Vue-aware toast with VNode icons, and custom() for VNodes."
  pageTitle="Vue"
>
  <p>
    <span class="tier helper">Helper</span>
    Vue 3 helper export with optional Toaster, Vue-aware <code>toast</code>, and <code>custom()</code> for VNodes.
    For a live demo and install snippet, see the <a href="/vue">Vue landing</a>.
  </p>

  <pre class="api"><code>{`<script setup>
import { toast, Toaster, custom } from "alert-notify/vue";
import { h } from "vue";
</script>

<template>
  <Toaster position="top-right" :rich-colors="true" />
  <button @click="toast.success('Saved')">Save</button>
  <button
    @click="
      toast.info('Pay with card', {
        icon: h('img', { src: '/card.png', alt: '' }),
      })
    "
  >
    With icon
  </button>
  <button @click="custom(h('div', 'Custom Vue content'))">Custom</button>
</template>`}</code></pre>

  <ul class="notes">
    <li>Peer dependency: vue &gt;= 3.</li>
    <li>Import <code>toast</code> from <code>alert-notify/vue</code> when passing VNode icons.</li>
    <li>Landing page: <a href="/vue">/vue</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
